    "framePromptBlock": "prefer(experiencer, theme; experiencer: actor|entity|system) — An experiencer has a preference for a theme.\nsend(agent, object; optional: recipient, destination; recipient|destination (mutually exclusive); agent: actor|entity|system; recipient: actor|entity|system) — An agent transmits an object to a recipient or destination.\nreceive(recipient, theme; optional: source; recipient: actor|entity|system) — A recipient accepts or receives a theme from a source.\nbelieve(experiencer, theme; experiencer: actor|entity|system) — An experiencer holds a belief regarding a theme or proposition.\npublish(agent, theme; optional: audience; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent makes a theme available to an audience or public.\nretry(agent; optional: count, theme; at least one of: count|theme; agent: actor|entity|system; count: quantity) — An agent attempts an action again, with a count or action theme.\nrequest(agent, theme; optional: recipient; agent: actor|entity|system; recipient: actor|entity|system) — An agent requests a theme or action from an optional recipient.\nkeep(no required roles; optional: agent, theme, visibility; at least one of: theme|visibility; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent retains a theme, optionally with an explicit visibility.\ndelete(no required roles; optional: agent, theme, object, target; theme|object|target (mutually exclusive); agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent removes or deletes an object/theme/target.\nenable(theme; optional: agent; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent enables a feature, system, or capability.\ndisable(theme; optional: agent; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent disables a feature, system, or capability.\nallow(agent, theme; optional: recipient; agent: actor|entity|system; recipient: actor|entity|system) — An agent permits a recipient to perform an action or access a theme.\nprohibit(agent, theme; optional: recipient; agent: actor|entity|system; recipient: actor|entity|system) — An agent forbids a recipient from performing an action or accessing a theme.\ndeploy(agent, destination; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent deploys to an environment or destination.\ncopy(agent, source, destination; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent copies a resource from source to destination.\nrotate(agent, theme; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent rotates a credential or key.\ndeadline(subject, time) — A subject has a deadline at time.\nbelow(subject, value) — A metric or subject is below a threshold or value.\nabove(subject, value) — A metric or subject is above a threshold or value.\nbefore(subject, object) — A subject event precedes an object event.\nafter(subject, object) — A subject event follows an object event.\nconfirmed(no required roles; optional: agent, theme; at least one of: agent|theme; agent: actor|entity|system) — An action or transaction is confirmed by an agent or for a theme.\nconfirm(no required roles; optional: agent, theme; at least one of: agent|theme; agent: actor|entity|system) — An agent confirms an action or transaction.",
    "roleValues": "Use typed LunumTerm objects with the field name type (never termType). Identifier terms use id or ref; literal terms use value. The builder rejects missing or disallowed types, missing required roles, extra roles, and exclusive-role conflicts.",
